When you scale covariates in a Bayesian context, this will meaningfully change your priors unless the priors have been scaled equivalently. If the scaling is dramatic I could see an equivalent "noninformative" prior yielding pretty different posteriors. Could that explain what you're seeing?

Another thing I'd be curious about is the effective sample size of the parameter estimates.

Ben

