Hi Shari. I agree with your phrasing as well as your assessment of your co-author's alternative. Your co-authors phrasing makes it sound like you're talking about occupancy by the species of the whole region rather than a given sampling unit within that region. A compromise might be "Gibbons were more likely to occupy Kerangas sampling units than those in Low Pole."

